  "upstream": [
    "CVE-2026-15176",
    "CVE-2026-56434"
  ],
  "published": "2026-10-20T09:12:52Z",
  "modified": "2026-10-20T09:12:52Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap buffer overflow when mapping a rewritten URI to a\n     path in a location using alias\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-15176.patch: reject URI to path mapping in\n       ngx_http_map_uri_to_path() when r->uri_changed is set, so a rewrite\n       that shortens the URI below the alias location prefix can no longer\n       overflow the path buffer through $request_filename\n     - CVE-2026-15176\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: use-after-free via duplicate subrequest finalization\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-56434.patch: skip posting a request in\n       ngx_http_post_request() if it is already posted, and reset the\n       subrequest write event handler during finalization in\n       ngx_http_finalize_request(), so an SSI subrequest double-posted during\n       unbuffered proxying can no longer be finalized twice\n     - CVE-2026-56434",
